# Birthday scenes for all twelve villagers (T-107): one choice each, a gift back, a thank-you letter after and a letter if the player missed it. Compiled to zz_fs_birthdays.json.

dialogue wren.birthday
n0 wren: Now. Between us, I expect a toast. What's it going to be?
  ? Raise a glass to her. => r0 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.bday.wren.glass
  ? Sing something badly. => r1 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.bday.wren.sing
  ? Give her a quiet hug. => r2 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.bday.wren.hug
r0 wren: To me! Oh, the best toast I've had all year, and I wrote the other ones.
  expr happy
r1 wren: That was dreadful. Do it again, louder. The glasses are rattling in protest.
  expr happy
r2 wren: Oh. ...Oh, you're a menace. A kind one. Sit down before I embarrass us both.
  expr happy

dialogue hazel.birthday
n0 hazel: (You came anyway.) What happens now?
  ? Wish her a happy birthday. => r0 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.bday.hazel.wish
  ? Read her a line from her favorite book. => r1 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.bday.hazel.read
  ? Sit with her in silence. => r2 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.bday.hazel.sit
r0 hazel: Two words, said kindly. (I counted. I always count.) I'll keep them.
  expr happy
r1 hazel: That one. (You remembered.) I need a moment. The lighthouse keeper would understand.
  expr embarrassed
r2 hazel: (Nobody is singing.) This is the best present. Please stay until the cake is gone.
  expr happy

dialogue bram.birthday
n0 bram: You came. Well?
  ? Wish him a good year. => r0 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bday.bram.wish
  ? Hand him a small gift. => r1 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bday.bram.gift
  ? Sit on the bench with him. => r2 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bday.bram.bench
r0 bram: A good year. Hm. I'll forge one. Slowly.
  expr happy
r1 bram: ...Hm. For me? It goes on the shelf. Next to the card.
  expr happy
r2 bram: Hm. Left side. It's warmer. I checked.
  expr happy

dialogue tilda.birthday
n0 tilda: You looked at the slate. I saw. Go on, then. What do you say?
  ? Happy birthday, Tilda. => r0 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.bday.tilda.wish
  ? Give her a flower. => r1 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.bday.tilda.flower
  ? Mind the shop. Go read. => r2 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.bday.tilda.mind
r0 tilda: Oh. Well. That goes at the top of the slate, where I'll see it first thing every morning.
  expr happy
r1 tilda: A flower, in my shop! It goes in the window, beside the good pumpkin.
  expr happy
r2 tilda: You'd mind it? That's the best present. Take the stool. The cat bites coins, not customers.
  expr happy

dialogue juno.birthday
n0 juno: So? What's the plan? There's a plan, right? Tell me there's a plan!
  ? Wish her a happy birthday. => r0 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.bday.juno.wish
  ? 'Cake (Birthday)'? Really? => r1 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.bday.juno.tease
  ? Slip her a tiny gift. => r2 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.bday.juno.gift
r0 juno: Thank you! I'm framing that. The actual words. I'll need a very thin frame.
  expr happy
r1 juno: It's a perfectly good label! ...Okay, it's too good. I'm going red. That's the forge.
  expr embarrassed
r2 juno: A gift! For me! On purpose! I'm going to cry on a clasp. Again.
  expr happy

dialogue piper.birthday
n0 piper: Front row's yours. Now give me your best line!
  ? Wish her a happy birthday. => r0 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.bday.piper.wish
  ? Sing her song back to her. => r1 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.bday.piper.sing
  ? Ask what the next song is. => r2 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.bday.piper.ask
r0 piper: Happy birthday to me, from you! Short, sweet, and in tune. It's going in the encore.
  expr happy
r1 piper: You sang my song! Back to me! ...I'm keeping your key. It's mine now.
  expr happy
r2 piper: The next one's yours. It isn't finished. It's a birthday present on a musician's schedule.
  expr happy

dialogue marcus.birthday
n0 marcus: The bench holds two. What do you say?
  ? Happy birthday, Marcus. => r0 | friend:marcus,10 | flag:choice.bday.marcus.wish
  ? That's a beautiful plank. => r1 | friend:marcus,10 | flag:choice.bday.marcus.plank
  ? Need someone on the other end? => r2 | friend:marcus,10 | flag:choice.bday.marcus.hold
r0 marcus: Thank you. I'll write that on the beam, small, where only I'll look.
  expr happy
r1 marcus: Oak. Straight grain, no knots. Most people see a board. You saw the grain.
  expr happy
r2 marcus: The other end. Yes. A second pair of hands is the best present there is.
  expr happy

dialogue odalys.birthday
n0 odalys: You stayed. I have no protocol for this. What now?
  ? Wish her a happy birthday. => r0 | friend:odalys,10 | flag:choice.bday.odalys.wish
  ? Pull up a chair for the soup. => r1 | friend:odalys,10 | flag:choice.bday.odalys.soup
  ? Prescribe her an afternoon nap. => r2 | friend:odalys,10 | flag:choice.bday.odalys.nap
r0 odalys: ...Thank you. Most people wish me well by not needing me today. This is better.
  expr happy
r1 odalys: Then pass your bowl. Leek and potato, and an irresponsible amount of pepper. It's my birthday.
  expr happy
r2 odalys: A nap, prescribed by a farmer. ...Very well. My patients will be told it was an emergency.
  expr happy

dialogue felix.birthday
n0 felix: The story can wait. What's the word?
  ? Wish him a happy birthday. => r0 | friend:felix,10 | flag:choice.bday.felix.wish
  ? Ask for the fish story. => r1 | friend:felix,10 | flag:choice.bday.felix.story
  ? Offer to fish with him. => r2 | friend:felix,10 | flag:choice.bday.felix.fish
r0 felix: Kind of you. I'll tell the fish. They won't care, but I'll feel taller.
  expr happy
r1 felix: Sit, then. It was dawn, it was this big, and it was smirking at me.
  expr happy
r2 felix: Dawn tomorrow. Bring a line. I'll bring the good rock.
  expr happy

dialogue dorian.birthday
n0 dorian: ...You stayed. What now?
  ? Wish him a quiet happy birthday. => r0 | friend:dorian,10 | flag:choice.bday.dorian.wish
  ? Offer a slow walk in the forest. => r1 | friend:dorian,10 | flag:choice.bday.dorian.walk
  ? Hand him a perfect pinecone. => r2 | friend:dorian,10 | flag:choice.bday.dorian.cone
r0 dorian: ...Thank you. Said quietly. That's the right size.
  expr happy
r1 dorian: Good. There's a spot where the moss is thick.
  expr happy
r2 dorian: Closed tight. Perfect. ...I'm keeping it.
  expr embarrassed

dialogue elara.birthday
n0 elara: You came! What do we do first?
  ? Happy birthday, Elara! => r0 | friend:elara,10 | flag:choice.bday.elara.wish
  ? That hat is magnificent. Both of them. => r1 | friend:elara,10 | flag:choice.bday.elara.hat
  ? Beach day. Bring the hat's hat. => r2 | friend:elara,10 | flag:choice.bday.elara.beach
r0 elara: Thank you! I'm knitting that into my scarf. Every word. In red.
  expr happy
r1 elara: You noticed the small hat! Nobody notices the small hat! I'm so happy I might need a lie-down!
  expr happy
r2 elara: The beach! On my birthday! Yes! Dr. Penn can mind the plant. I'm bringing the hat's hat, and a towel!
  expr happy

dialogue ione.birthday
n0 ione: The new book can wait. It's very patient. What shall we do?
  ? Wish her the happiest of birthdays. => r0 | friend:ione,10 | flag:choice.bday.ione.wish
  ? Read the first page to her. => r1 | friend:ione,10 | flag:choice.bday.ione.read
  ? Give her a bookmark. A slightly crooked one. => r2 | friend:ione,10 | flag:choice.bday.ione.mark
r0 ione: Thank you. I'll keep that between two good pages, where I'll come across it often.
  expr happy
r1 ione: The first page, aloud. Nobody's read to me since I was small. I'll close my eyes, if you don't mind.
  expr happy
r2 ione: A bookmark. From you. It's crooked. So is my favorite book. They'll get along.
  expr happy
